(*****************************************************************)
(*  WARNINGS — branches the model may not follow as Rust does.   *)
(*                                                               *)
(*  Each `HAX WARNING` below marks an `if` or `match` on a value *)
(*  the model cannot always evaluate. When it cannot, no arm of  *)
(*  a `match` is taken (the trace ends) and an `if` takes its    *)
(*  `else` branch, whatever Rust does. A query about the other   *)
(*  branch may then hold for lack of any trace.                  *)
(*                                                               *)
(*  - 1 × `replace_body` keeps the `&mut` parameters `st` unchanged *)
(*  - 1 × branch on an ordering comparison, which the model decides only between literals up to 16 *)
(*  - 1 × `core__str__converts__from_utf8` returns a `Result` but has no model: unless its declaration in missingdecl.pvl is replaced by one returning `hax_result_ok(..)` or `hax_result_err(..)`, every path through its uses is lost *)
(*  - 1 × branch on a result of `core__str__converts__from_utf8`, which the model does not define *)
(*  - 3 × `pv_unchecked_results`: the uses of `Result` in this function are not checked against the Result model *)
(*  - 1 × `core__result__Impl_3__transpose` returns a `Result` but has no model: unless its declaration in missingdecl.pvl is replaced by one returning `hax_result_ok(..)` or `hax_result_err(..)`, every path through its uses is lost *)
(*  - 1 × `rust_primitives__hax__deref_op` returns a `Result` but has no model: unless its declaration in missingdecl.pvl is replaced by one returning `hax_result_ok(..)` or `hax_result_err(..)`, every path through its uses is lost *)
(*  - 2 × `new_tests__legacy__proverif_result_errors__lib__Kept__dec` is a kept trait call returning a `Result`: unless its hand-written model returns `hax_result_ok(..)` or `hax_result_err(..)`, every path through its uses is lost *)
(*****************************************************************)

